Let reagents/tools auto-banked into the account-wide vault still count
as "in your backpack" when crafting, instead of needing a manual
withdraw first.
Touches: src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp, Spell::CheckCast()

Why: reagents and profession tools now auto-bank into the account vault
(ACT_REAGENT_VAULT, LivingGear_Vault.cpp), which is exactly what "reagent
bank should also include tool items... consider them as contained in your
backpack so you can craft wherever you want" asked for -- but the vault
itself is just DB-backed bookkeeping with zero connection to the real
crafting system. Without this patch, the engine's own reagent check
(player->HasItemCount(itemid, itemcount, true)) only ever sees the
player's actual bags, so anything banked became invisible to crafting --
profession windows showed the reagent as known/available (client-side
count comes from a different source) but casting the actual craft spell
failed with SPELL_FAILED_REAGENTS every time.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
@@ (near the top, alongside the existing Living Gear forward-declares)
 bool LivingGear_BypassStealthRequirement(Unit* caster);
+void LivingGear_TopUpReagentFromVault(Player* player, uint32 itemId, uint32 needed);

@@ Spell::CheckCast(bool strict) -- inside the MAX_SPELL_REAGENTS loop
-                if (!player->HasItemCount(itemid, itemcount, true))
+                LivingGear_TopUpReagentFromVault(player, itemid, itemcount);
+                if (!player->HasItemCount(itemid, itemcount, true))
                     return SPELL_FAILED_REAGENTS;

LivingGear_TopUpReagentFromVault (LivingGear_Vault.cpp) checks the
player's current bag count against what's needed; if short, withdraws
just the shortfall from the account-wide reagent vault into the bag
(putting it back if the bag turns out to be full) -- the engine's own
HasItemCount check right after then passes normally, and normal
consumption/inventory logic handles the rest completely unmodified.
